+# 020: Bulk-delete guard with a small-vault floor, batch pre-check and system exemption
+
+Status: accepted
+
+Date: 2026-10-11
+
+Source: [M3 proposal](../../internal/core/M3-core-namespace-proposal.md), decision D6.
+
+## Context
+
+The specification rejects more than 25 deletes, or more than 10% of live files,
+from one device within 5 minutes unless confirmed. As written it has three
+problems. In a 6-file vault, one delete is 17% and trips the guard. A per-
+submission check commits the first 25 deletes of a 40-file folder and rejects
+the rest, leaving a half-deleted folder. And the Canvas bridge, removing a
+course's PDFs, would be blocked by a guard meant for misconfigured devices.
+
+## Decision
+
+- `limit(live) = min(25, max(5, floor(0.10 × live)))`. A check trips when the
+  unconfirmed deletes recorded in the window plus the batch exceed the limit.
+- Confirmed deletes are not recorded. A tripped check changes no state.
+- Bridge and Admin actors are exempt. The bridge has its own rule: it never
+  touches user-owned files.
+- The guard is a pure value (`rules.DeleteGuard`) with a fixed ring of 10-second
+  buckets; expiry rounds against the user. The server checks each submission
+  with a batch of 1. The plugin runs the same function with the real batch size
+  before sending the first delete and asks once, up front.
+
+Rejected: the original formula (blocks small vaults); per-submission checking
+alone (half-deleted folders); deriving counts from the change feed on every
+delete (a query per delete for a 5-minute window).
+
+## Consequences
+
+Small vaults can delete a few files without a dialog, large vaults keep the
+25-delete ceiling, and a folder delete is either confirmed up front or not sent.
+If plugin and server states disagree, the server's reject stops the remainder
+and the plugin asks for those. Guard state lives in engine memory and resets on
+restart, allowing up to one more window of unconfirmed deletes per restart.
+Invariant 7's pull-only first sync remains the primary defense; this is the
+backstop.
